    { q: 'What is the difference between an awning and a porch?', a: 'An awning protects the doorway without adding a porch footprint or floor, and starts at $900. A porch creates covered space you can stand or sit in, with its own supports and decking.' },
    { q: 'Do porches or dormers need a permit?', a: 'They can. Porches, awnings and dormers may change a building’s footprint, projection or height, and rules vary across Ohio, Northern Kentucky and Southeast Indiana. Confirm the requirements for your address before finalizing the design.' },
    { q: 'Are windows included in the dormer price?', a: 'No. Dormer prices cover the framing, roof integration, siding and trim. Windows are priced separately on the Windows & Natural Light page.' },
  ],
